<title>PHILIPPINES: Manila's PHIBOR rates slip across the board.</title>
<headline>Manila's PHIBOR rates slip across the board.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1996-10-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Philippine interbank offered rates (PHIBOR) slipped across all maturities on Wednesday, traders said.</p>
<p>The continued liquidity in the money market encouraged banks to lower their swap rates at the PHIBOR market, traders said.</p>
<p>&quot;It's still liquid enough to withstand the Central Bank's huge dollar sales yesterday,&quot; one dealer said.</p>
<p>The Central bank's dollar sales effectively lessen  banks' peso liquidity.</p>
<p>PHIBOR represents rates at which banks are willing to swap their pesos for dollars.  </p>
<p>Average rates quoted by 20 banks were:</p>
<p>			  OCT 16		 OCT 15</p>
<p>    1 W		11  7/16		11  5/8</p>
<p>    2 W		11  7/16		11  9/16</p>
<p>    1 M		11  7/16		11  1/2</p>
<p>    2 M		11  7/16		11  1/2</p>
<p>    3 M		11  1/2		 11  9/16</p>
<p>    6 M		11  3/4		 11  3/4</p>
<p>    12M		11 13/16		11  7/8</p>
<p>    VAL		17-Oct		  16-Oct</p>
<p>- LILIAN KARUNUNGAN (632) 841-8937</p>
